{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Etzrb5sjBeXZ2P97kdJ17g","type":"tool_result","content":"package closeout\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/committer\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/redact\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// recordVersion stays 1 across the Reaper's additions (Job.Cause, Plan.Tail,\n// Plan.TailWithheld, Plan.KeepUntil) and the usage-limit ones (Cause.Family,\n// Cause.ResetsAt, OutcomeLimited) and the network one (Plan.Network,\n// OutcomeNeedsNetwork) and Job.Home: older records decode them as zero, and\n// zero means the earlier behaviour.\nconst recordVersion = 1\n\n// RecordVersion is the version of the stored close-out record, for tests that\n// seed records.\nconst RecordVersion = recordVersion\n\n// failedKeep is how long a failed job's resources are kept (proposal: 24 h).\nconst failedKeep = 24 * time.Hour\n\n// Job is everything close-out needs, built by the caller from the state job\n// and the executor handle. It is persisted inside the Record, so Resume needs\n// nothing else.\ntype Job struct {\n\tID       string // ULID\n\tIssue    int    // negative only in dry-run\n\tPR       int    // 0 until a PR exists; required for a review\n\tStage    string // triage | worker | review\n\tRole     string\n\tAttempt  int\n\tBranch   string // \"\" commits to main (triage); worker/<name> otherwise\n\tWorktree string // executor handle Worktree\n\t// Home is the executor handle Home: the job's host home dir (its config\n\t// dir, TMPDIR and sidecar live under it). \"\" on a record stored before\n\t// #156; the redactor then skips that cosmetic rule.\n\tHome    string\n\tBaseSHA string // executor handle BaseSHA: what the worktree started from\n\tLogPath string // executor handle LogPath; \"\" when there is no log\n\t// Scrubbed is copied from the executor handle: the paths it removed from\n\t// the worktree before the agent ran. An unchanged role file is trusted\n\t// only if listed here.\n\tScrubbed []string\n\tExitCode int\n\tCostUSD  float64 // 0 when unknown\n\t// Cause, when Kind is set, says why the job ended without a usable result.\n\t// Close-out then skips the role file and the changed files and commits only\n\t// the log. The zero Cause decides from the role file and exit code.\n\tCause Cause\n\t// Worker is the worker loop's result: the PR, reviewers and test outcome.\n\t// nil for every other job; a done worker job without it needs a human.\n\tWorker *WorkerResult\n\t// ExtraLogs are further host logs to redact and commit beside LogPath: the\n\t// earlier agent steps of a worker job. A withheld one holds the job.\n\tExtraLogs []string\n\t// Review is the reviewer loop's context: the added lines for inline\n\t// placement and whether the PR head moved. nil for every other job, and\n\t// for a review closed out by the Reaper after a restart.\n\tReview *ReviewContext\n\t// Usage is the job's agent usage summed over its steps (from state). The\n\t// zero value renders as \"not reported\".\n\tUsage Usage\n\t// TokensUnreported is set when the job's final agent step ended without\n\t// reporting tokens: its token use is not counted, so the day's token count\n\t// for the role is low. The close-out comment and cost-table row say so.\n\tTokensUnreported bool `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\t// StartedAt is when the job was created; zero when unknown.\n\tStartedAt time.Time\n}\n\n// Tokens are token counts by type; it mirrors state.Tokens.\ntype Tokens struct{ Input, Output, CacheWrite, CacheRead int64 }\n\n// Usage is the job's agent usage summed over its steps (from state).\ntype Usage struct {\n\tModels  []string `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tTokens  *Tokens  `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tCostUSD *float64 `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tSteps   int      `json:\",omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CauseKind names why a job ended without a usable result.\ntype CauseKind string\n\n// Cause kinds. The reason in the comment is \"<kind>: <detail>\".\nconst (\n\tCauseQuiet     CauseKind = \"heartbeat_quiet\"    // no log output for 10 minutes\n\tCauseDeadline  CauseKind = \"deadline\"           // ran past its timeout\n\tCauseRestart   CauseKind = \"controller_restart\" // orphaned, gone or never started across a restart\n\tCauseNoProcess CauseKind = \"no_process\"         // never started, or its process vanished in this run\n\tCauseRateLimit CauseKind = \"rate_limit\"         // the agent reported a transient API error\n\tCauseCloneFail CauseKind = \"clone_failed\"       // a loop's Prepare failed at git or clone\n\t// CauseUsageLimit: the run stopped at a subscription usage limit. It is\n\t// not a failure and never hands off to the automatic retry (Retry is\n\t// false); the issue is re-claimed after the reset.\n\tCauseUsageLimit CauseKind = \"usage_limit\"\n)\n\n// Cause is why a job ended. Detail is fixed, non-secret text.\ntype Cause struct {\n\tKind      CauseKind\n\tDetail    string\n\tTransient bool // a named transient cause\n\tRetry     bool // hand off to one automatic retry: Transient and the job is not itself a retry\n\t// Family and ResetsAt are for CauseUsageLimit only. Family is the model\n\t// family the limit names (\"\" is the whole account). ResetsAt is when the\n\t// pause ends: the Finisher fills it from the limits book, so it is never\n\t// zero by the time close-out sees it.\n\tFamily   string\n\tResetsAt time.Time\n}\n\n// ErrBusy means another close-out of the same job is in flight. Run and\n// ResumeJob wrap it; callers skip quietly and look again later.\nvar ErrBusy = errors.New(\"closeout: another close-out of this job is in flight\")\n\n// Phase is how far close-out got.\ntype Phase string\n\nconst (\n\tPhasePrepared  Phase = \"prepared\"\n\tPhaseCommitted Phase = \"committed\"\n\tPhaseRequested Phase = \"requested\"\n\tPhaseCommented Phase = \"commented\"\n\tPhaseClosed    Phase = \"closed\"\n)\n\n// Record is the persisted state of one close-out.\ntype Record struct {\n\tVersion   int\n\tPhase     Phase\n\tJob       Job\n\tPlan      Plan\n\tSHA       string\n\tSynthetic bool // the commit was a dry-run: nothing reached the remote\n\tCommentID int64\n\t// ReviewMode says how a review reached GitHub (Review* constants).\n\tReviewMode string\n}\n\n// Effects is the subset of effects.Effects close-out uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tAddLabels(ctx context.Context, n int, labels ...string) error\n\tRemoveLabel(ctx context.Context, n int, label string) error\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tCreateReview(ctx context.Context, n int, in github.ReviewInput) (int64, error)\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Comments lists existing comments (github.Reader).\ntype Comments interface {\n\tListComments(ctx context.Context, n int, since time.Time) ([]github.Comment, error)\n\tListReviews(ctx context.Context, n int) ([]github.Review, error)\n}\n\n// Committer commits a file set to main (branch \"\") or a PR branch.\ntype Committer interface {\n\tCommit(ctx context.Context, branch string, req committer.Request) (committer.Result, error)\n}\n\n// Redactor is *redact.Redactor.\ntype Redactor interface {\n\tLog(ctx context.Context, src, dst string) (redact.LogResult, error)\n\tText(ctx context.Context, b []byte) (redact.TextResult, error)\n}\n\n// Store is the part of state.Store close-out uses.\ntype Store interface {\n\tFailRetry(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tFailLimited(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tJob(ctx context.Context, id string) (state.Job, error)\n\tSetCloseout(ctx context.Context, id, phase string, plan json.RawMessage) error\n\tOpenCloseouts(ctx context.Context) ([]state.Job, error)\n\tComplete(ctx context.Context, id string, costUSD *float64) error\n\tFail(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n}\n\n// Deferred returns the review requests that triage jobs of an issue recorded\n// but could not apply (no PR existed yet), de-duplicated, in request order. The\n// Phase 1 worker loop calls it when it opens the PR and adds the\n// ard:review:<role> labels to the PR itself. Only closed, done triage\n// close-outs count.\nfunc Deferred(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue int) ([]NextReq, error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"deferred reviewers of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tseen := map[NextReq]bool{}\n\tvar out []NextReq\n\tfor _, sj := range jobs {\n\t\trec, err := decode(sj)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || rec.Plan.Outcome != OutcomeDone {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, r := range rec.Plan.Deferred {\n\t\t\tif !seen[r] {\n\t\t\t\tseen[r] = true\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, r)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, nil\n}\n\n// LeadWorker returns the validated worker choice of the newest closed, done\n// triage:lead close-out of issue, and that job's id. ok is false when there is\n// none. worker is \"\" when that lead named no valid worker. The triage fan-in\n// gate reads the choice here, not from the committed role file, which a later\n// triage agent could rewrite.\nfunc LeadWorker(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue int) (worker, jobID string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"lead worker of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor _, sj := range jobs {\n\t\trec, err := decode(sj)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"lead worker of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != \"lead\" || rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || rec.Plan.Outcome != OutcomeDone {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tworker, jobID, ok = rec.Plan.Worker, rec.Job.ID, true\n\t}\n\treturn worker, jobID, ok, nil\n}\n\n// ReviewPassed returns the commit the newest closed review close-out of role\n// on PR pr approved, ok only when that close-out finished with outcome done,\n// carries a review plan and the head had not moved during the review. The\n// merger trusts this record, not the :done label, which a person with triage\n// access can add.\nfunc ReviewPassed(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue, pr int, role string) (sha string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageReview)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor i := len(jobs) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n\t\trec, err := decode(jobs[i])\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != role || rec.Job.PR != pr {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tp := rec.Plan\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || p.Outcome != OutcomeDone || p.Review == nil || p.Review.HeadMoved || p.Review.CommitSHA == \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn p.Review.CommitSHA, true, nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", false, nil\n}\n\n// ReviewChanged returns the commit the newest closed review close-out of role\n// on PR pr asked changes for, ok only when that close-out finished with\n// outcome changes and carries a review plan. A :changes label alone does not\n// count: a person with triage access can add it.\nfunc ReviewChanged(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue, pr int, role string) (sha string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageReview)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor i := len(jobs) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n\t\trec, err := decode(jobs[i])\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != role || rec.Job.PR != pr {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tp := rec.Plan\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || p.Outcome != OutcomeChanges || p.Review == nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn p.Review.CommitSHA, true, nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", false, nil\n}\n\n// Deps are the collaborators of a Closer. Prepare needs Roles, NewRedactor,\n// Changed, BaseFile and StagingDir; the rest are for Closer.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tEffects   Effects\n\tComments  Comments\n\tCommitter Committer\n\tStore     Store\n\tRoles     RoleSet\n\t// NewRedactor builds the redactor for a job, with the executor's secret\n\t// values (rebuilt, never persisted). Resume does not call it: it uses\n\t// only already-redacted staged bytes.\n\tNewRedactor func(Job) (Redactor, error)\n\t// Changed lists paths under a pathspec changed since a base commit\n\t// (gitx.Git.ChangedSince).\n\tChanged func(ctx context.Context, worktree, base string, paths ...string) ([]gitx.PathChange, error)\n\t// BaseFile reads one file at a commit (gitx.Git.FileAt): ok is false when\n\t// the path does not exist there. Prepare uses it to compare plan.md with\n\t// its base.\n\tBaseFile func(ctx context.Context, worktree, rev, path string, maxBytes int64) (data []byte, ok bool, err error)\n\t// PR reads a pull request (github.Reader.GetPR). Optional: a review's\n\t// close-out uses it to notice a PR merged or closed mid-review. nil skips\n\t// the check.\n\tPR         func(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.PullRequest, error)\n\tRepo       github.Repo\n\tStagingDir string","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"810fcc1c-bd8c-400e-9091-18198e00ee90","uuid":"b9c163bd-fe27-4d76-8135-9ce454ce61e6","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13:09:07.805Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"package closeout\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/committer\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/redact\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\n// recordVersion stays 1 across the Reaper's additions (Job.Cause, Plan.Tail,\n// Plan.TailWithheld, Plan.KeepUntil) and the usage-limit ones (Cause.Family,\n// Cause.ResetsAt, OutcomeLimited) and the network one (Plan.Network,\n// OutcomeNeedsNetwork) and Job.Home: older records decode them as zero, and\n// zero means the earlier behaviour.\nconst recordVersion = 1\n\n// RecordVersion is the version of the stored close-out record, for tests that\n// seed records.\nconst RecordVersion = recordVersion\n\n// failedKeep is how long a failed job's resources are kept (proposal: 24 h).\nconst failedKeep = 24 * time.Hour\n\n// Job is everything close-out needs, built by the caller from the state job\n// and the executor handle. It is persisted inside the Record, so Resume needs\n// nothing else.\ntype Job struct {\n\tID       string // ULID\n\tIssue    int    // negative only in dry-run\n\tPR       int    // 0 until a PR exists; required for a review\n\tStage    string // triage | worker | review\n\tRole     string\n\tAttempt  int\n\tBranch   string // \"\" commits to main (triage); worker/<name> otherwise\n\tWorktree string // executor handle Worktree\n\t// Home is the executor handle Home: the job's host home dir (its config\n\t// dir, TMPDIR and sidecar live under it). \"\" on a record stored before\n\t// #156; the redactor then skips that cosmetic rule.\n\tHome    string\n\tBaseSHA string // executor handle BaseSHA: what the worktree started from\n\tLogPath string // executor handle LogPath; \"\" when there is no log\n\t// Scrubbed is copied from the executor handle: the paths it removed from\n\t// the worktree before the agent ran. An unchanged role file is trusted\n\t// only if listed here.\n\tScrubbed []string\n\tExitCode int\n\tCostUSD  float64 // 0 when unknown\n\t// Cause, when Kind is set, says why the job ended without a usable result.\n\t// Close-out then skips the role file and the changed files and commits only\n\t// the log. The zero Cause decides from the role file and exit code.\n\tCause Cause\n\t// Worker is the worker loop's result: the PR, reviewers and test outcome.\n\t// nil for every other job; a done worker job without it needs a human.\n\tWorker *WorkerResult\n\t// ExtraLogs are further host logs to redact and commit beside LogPath: the\n\t// earlier agent steps of a worker job. A withheld one holds the job.\n\tExtraLogs []string\n\t// Review is the reviewer loop's context: the added lines for inline\n\t// placement and whether the PR head moved. nil for every other job, and\n\t// for a review closed out by the Reaper after a restart.\n\tReview *ReviewContext\n\t// Usage is the job's agent usage summed over its steps (from state). The\n\t// zero value renders as \"not reported\".\n\tUsage Usage\n\t// TokensUnreported is set when the job's final agent step ended without\n\t// reporting tokens: its token use is not counted, so the day's token count\n\t// for the role is low. The close-out comment and cost-table row say so.\n\tTokensUnreported bool `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\t// StartedAt is when the job was created; zero when unknown.\n\tStartedAt time.Time\n}\n\n// Tokens are token counts by type; it mirrors state.Tokens.\ntype Tokens struct{ Input, Output, CacheWrite, CacheRead int64 }\n\n// Usage is the job's agent usage summed over its steps (from state).\ntype Usage struct {\n\tModels  []string `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tTokens  *Tokens  `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tCostUSD *float64 `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tSteps   int      `json:\",omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CauseKind names why a job ended without a usable result.\ntype CauseKind string\n\n// Cause kinds. The reason in the comment is \"<kind>: <detail>\".\nconst (\n\tCauseQuiet     CauseKind = \"heartbeat_quiet\"    // no log output for 10 minutes\n\tCauseDeadline  CauseKind = \"deadline\"           // ran past its timeout\n\tCauseRestart   CauseKind = \"controller_restart\" // orphaned, gone or never started across a restart\n\tCauseNoProcess CauseKind = \"no_process\"         // never started, or its process vanished in this run\n\tCauseRateLimit CauseKind = \"rate_limit\"         // the agent reported a transient API error\n\tCauseCloneFail CauseKind = \"clone_failed\"       // a loop's Prepare failed at git or clone\n\t// CauseUsageLimit: the run stopped at a subscription usage limit. It is\n\t// not a failure and never hands off to the automatic retry (Retry is\n\t// false); the issue is re-claimed after the reset.\n\tCauseUsageLimit CauseKind = \"usage_limit\"\n)\n\n// Cause is why a job ended. Detail is fixed, non-secret text.\ntype Cause struct {\n\tKind      CauseKind\n\tDetail    string\n\tTransient bool // a named transient cause\n\tRetry     bool // hand off to one automatic retry: Transient and the job is not itself a retry\n\t// Family and ResetsAt are for CauseUsageLimit only. Family is the model\n\t// family the limit names (\"\" is the whole account). ResetsAt is when the\n\t// pause ends: the Finisher fills it from the limits book, so it is never\n\t// zero by the time close-out sees it.\n\tFamily   string\n\tResetsAt time.Time\n}\n\n// ErrBusy means another close-out of the same job is in flight. Run and\n// ResumeJob wrap it; callers skip quietly and look again later.\nvar ErrBusy = errors.New(\"closeout: another close-out of this job is in flight\")\n\n// Phase is how far close-out got.\ntype Phase string\n\nconst (\n\tPhasePrepared  Phase = \"prepared\"\n\tPhaseCommitted Phase = \"committed\"\n\tPhaseRequested Phase = \"requested\"\n\tPhaseCommented Phase = \"commented\"\n\tPhaseClosed    Phase = \"closed\"\n)\n\n// Record is the persisted state of one close-out.\ntype Record struct {\n\tVersion   int\n\tPhase     Phase\n\tJob       Job\n\tPlan      Plan\n\tSHA       string\n\tSynthetic bool // the commit was a dry-run: nothing reached the remote\n\tCommentID int64\n\t// ReviewMode says how a review reached GitHub (Review* constants).\n\tReviewMode string\n}\n\n// Effects is the subset of effects.Effects close-out uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tAddLabels(ctx context.Context, n int, labels ...string) error\n\tRemoveLabel(ctx context.Context, n int, label string) error\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tCreateReview(ctx context.Context, n int, in github.ReviewInput) (int64, error)\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Comments lists existing comments (github.Reader).\ntype Comments interface {\n\tListComments(ctx context.Context, n int, since time.Time) ([]github.Comment, error)\n\tListReviews(ctx context.Context, n int) ([]github.Review, error)\n}\n\n// Committer commits a file set to main (branch \"\") or a PR branch.\ntype Committer interface {\n\tCommit(ctx context.Context, branch string, req committer.Request) (committer.Result, error)\n}\n\n// Redactor is *redact.Redactor.\ntype Redactor interface {\n\tLog(ctx context.Context, src, dst string) (redact.LogResult, error)\n\tText(ctx context.Context, b []byte) (redact.TextResult, error)\n}\n\n// Store is the part of state.Store close-out uses.\ntype Store interface {\n\tFailRetry(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tFailLimited(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tJob(ctx context.Context, id string) (state.Job, error)\n\tSetCloseout(ctx context.Context, id, phase string, plan json.RawMessage) error\n\tOpenCloseouts(ctx context.Context) ([]state.Job, error)\n\tComplete(ctx context.Context, id string, costUSD *float64) error\n\tFail(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n}\n\n// Deferred returns the review requests that triage jobs of an issue recorded\n// but could not apply (no PR existed yet), de-duplicated, in request order. The\n// Phase 1 worker loop calls it when it opens the PR and adds the\n// ard:review:<role> labels to the PR itself. Only closed, done triage\n// close-outs count.\nfunc Deferred(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue int) ([]NextReq, error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"deferred reviewers of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tseen := map[NextReq]bool{}\n\tvar out []NextReq\n\tfor _, sj := range jobs {\n\t\trec, err := decode(sj)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || rec.Plan.Outcome != OutcomeDone {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, r := range rec.Plan.Deferred {\n\t\t\tif !seen[r] {\n\t\t\t\tseen[r] = true\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, r)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, nil\n}\n\n// LeadWorker returns the validated worker choice of the newest closed, done\n// triage:lead close-out of issue, and that job's id. ok is false when there is\n// none. worker is \"\" when that lead named no valid worker. The triage fan-in\n// gate reads the choice here, not from the committed role file, which a later\n// triage agent could rewrite.\nfunc LeadWorker(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue int) (worker, jobID string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"lead worker of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor _, sj := range jobs {\n\t\trec, err := decode(sj)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"lead worker of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != \"lead\" || rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || rec.Plan.Outcome != OutcomeDone {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tworker, jobID, ok = rec.Plan.Worker, rec.Job.ID, true\n\t}\n\treturn worker, jobID, ok, nil\n}\n\n// ReviewPassed returns the commit the newest closed review close-out of role\n// on PR pr approved, ok only when that close-out finished with outcome done,\n// carries a review plan and the head had not moved during the review. The\n// merger trusts this record, not the :done label, which a person with triage\n// access can add.\nfunc ReviewPassed(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue, pr int, role string) (sha string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageReview)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor i := len(jobs) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n\t\trec, err := decode(jobs[i])\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != role || rec.Job.PR != pr {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tp := rec.Plan\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || p.Outcome != OutcomeDone || p.Review == nil || p.Review.HeadMoved || p.Review.CommitSHA == \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn p.Review.CommitSHA, true, nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", false, nil\n}\n\n// ReviewChanged returns the commit the newest closed review close-out of role\n// on PR pr asked changes for, ok only when that close-out finished with\n// outcome changes and carries a review plan. A :changes label alone does not\n// count: a person with triage access can add it.\nfunc ReviewChanged(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n}, issue, pr int, role string) (sha string, ok bool, err error) {\n\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageReview)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t}\n\tfor i := len(jobs) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {\n\t\trec, err := decode(jobs[i])\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"review of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif rec.Job.Role != role || rec.Job.PR != pr {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tp := rec.Plan\n\t\tif rec.Phase != PhaseClosed || p.Outcome != OutcomeChanges || p.Review == nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn p.Review.CommitSHA, true, nil\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", false, nil\n}\n\n// Deps are the collaborators of a Closer. Prepare needs Roles, NewRedactor,\n// Changed, BaseFile and StagingDir; the rest are for Closer.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tEffects   Effects\n\tComments  Comments\n\tCommitter Committer\n\tStore     Store\n\tRoles     RoleSet\n\t// NewRedactor builds the redactor for a job, with the executor's secret\n\t// values (rebuilt, never persisted). Resume does not call it: it uses\n\t// only already-redacted staged bytes.\n\tNewRedactor func(Job) (Redactor, error)\n\t// Changed lists paths under a pathspec changed since a base commit\n\t// (gitx.Git.ChangedSince).\n\tChanged func(ctx context.Context, worktree, base string, paths ...string) ([]gitx.PathChange, error)\n\t// BaseFile reads one file at a commit (gitx.Git.FileAt): ok is false when\n\t// the path does not exist there. Prepare uses it to compare plan.md with\n\t// its base.\n\tBaseFile func(ctx context.Context, worktree, rev, path string, maxBytes int64) (data []byte, ok bool, err error)\n\t// PR reads a pull request (github.Reader.GetPR). Optional: a review's\n\t// close-out uses it to notice a PR merged or closed mid-review. nil skips\n\t// the check.\n\tPR         func(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.PullRequest, error)\n\tRepo       github.Repo\n\tStagingDir string","stderr":"","interrupted":f